13:13:26 | INFO | 🤖 Target: It’s understandable as a common-sense intuition: people drawn to abstract logic may be more likely to enjoy focused, intellectual, or niche pursuits. That can contribute to a recognizable “math person” culture. But it still doesn’t naturally follow that they will become “nerdy” in every sense people use that word. Being good at or interested in numbers doesn’t determine someone’s social skills, fashion, humor, relationships, hobbies, or connection to popular culture. Those develop through many influences besides their work. So you don’t need a study to notice patterns, but you also don’t need to treat the pattern as destiny. Your cousin may be nerdy, may not be, or may embrace some parts of that identity and not others. Since you know her personally, her actual preferences are better evidence than the occupational label.
